{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Information.PNeqNpEquivalence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Information.PNeqNpEquivalence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.counting_faithfulness_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.counting_faithfulness_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":262,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L262-L276","doc":"**End-to-end companion faithfulness, bridge discharged (sorry-free\nmodulo the two cited classes).**  For the real substrate\n$q_0 > 1$: given $\\mathrm{FP} \\neq \\#\\mathrm{P}$, exact Jones\nevaluation at $q_0$ is not polynomial-time.  The semisimplicity\nleg is *supplied* (Wenzl genericity from $q_0 > 1$), no longer\nassumed — and the obstruction residual does not appear: the\nreachable counting statement depends only on the genericity of the\nsubstrate parameter.  What remains open beyond citations is\nexactly the pair displayed by `faithfulness_of_transfer`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.semisimple_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.semisimple_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":256,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L256-L260","doc":"**Bridge discharged (sorry-free modulo the cited criterion).**\nFor real $q > 1$, $H_n(q)$ is semisimple at every rank. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion.semisimple_of_generic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion.semisimple_of_generic","kind":"theorem","line":254,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L254-L254","doc":"Wenzl's semisimplicity criterion, carried as a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion.mk","kind":"ctor","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L251-L251","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.WenzlCriterion","kind":"class","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L243-L254","doc":"**Cited Wenzl criterion** (hypothesis class, not a theorem of this\ndevelopment): parameter genericity implies semisimplicity of\n$H_n(q)$.  `semisimple n` is an opaque per-rank `Prop` pending the\nstage-2 Hecke radical formalisation (bean `qou-vndn`).  **No\ninstance is declared** — a fabricated instance would launder\n[wenzl1988] into a Lean proof.\n\nRef: [wenzl1988] https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01404457 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":235,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L235-L241","doc":"**The substrate is Wenzl-generic at every rank (sorry-free).**\nAny real $q > 1$ — in particular $q_0 \\approx 1.10998$ — satisfies\nthe Wenzl genericity condition for all $n$: the semisimplicity\n*hypothesis* is discharged by pure order arithmetic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_nontorsion","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_nontorsion","kind":"theorem","line":230,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L230-L233","doc":"Non-torsion implies Wenzl genericity at every rank (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.wenzlGeneric_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":225,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L225-L228","doc":"Genericity is antitone in the rank (sorry-free). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.WenzlGeneric","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.WenzlGeneric","kind":"def","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L216-L223","doc":"**Wenzl genericity** (parameter-side semisimplicity condition,\ngeneric monoid per §7c): `q` is not a `k`-th root of unity for any\n`2 ≤ k ≤ n`.  Equivalent to `[n]_q! ≠ 0` over a field; the form\nhere is the one Wenzl's criterion consumes.\n\nRef: [wenzl1988] https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01404457 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.faithfulness_of_transfer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.faithfulness_of_transfer","kind":"theorem","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L176-L197","doc":"**Isolation of the open kernel.**  The conjectured faithfulness\n($\\mathrm{res} \\neq 0 \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$)\nfollows from the cited layer + bridge + **two open inputs**, and\nthis theorem exists to display them:\n\n* `hFP` — the counting separation $\\mathrm{FP} \\neq \\#\\mathrm{P}$\n  itself (open; weaker than $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$ by\n  `counting_sep_of_decision_sep`), and\n* `transfer` — a counting$\\to$decision transfer\n  ($\\text{Jones} \\notin \\mathrm{FP} \\Rightarrow\n   \\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$), which **no known result\n  supplies**: $\\#\\mathrm{P}$-hardness of one invariant does not\n  imply $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$.\n\nDischarging these two hypotheses IS proving `conj:qou-p-neq-np`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.counting_faithfulness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.counting_faithfulness","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L166-L174","doc":"**Companion (counting) faithfulness — provable, unlike the\n$\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$ faithfulness.**  Given\n$\\mathrm{FP} \\neq \\#\\mathrm{P}$ and the bridge, a surviving residue\nforces exact Jones evaluation at $q_0$ out of $\\mathrm{FP}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.intractability_of_residual_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.intractability_of_residual_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**Composition (sorry-free modulo citations).**  Given the\nresidue–semisimplicity bridge (the open front (a), tracked as its\nown epic), a surviving residue makes polynomial-time exact Jones\nevaluation collapse $\\mathrm{FP} = \\#\\mathrm{P}$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.counting_sep_of_decision_sep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.counting_sep_of_decision_sep","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L148-L154","doc":"$\\mathrm{FP} \\neq \\#\\mathrm{P}$ is the *weaker* separation:\nit already follows from $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$ (sorry-free\ngiven the cited layer). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.counting_dominates_decision","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.counting_dominates_decision","kind":"theorem","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L144-L144","doc":"$\\mathrm{NP} \\subseteq \\mathrm{P}^{\\#\\mathrm{P}}$: if counting is\neasy, decision is easy.\n\nRef: [arora2009] https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9780511804090 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.jvw_sharp_p_hard","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.jvw_sharp_p_hard","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L139-L139","doc":"Jaeger--Vertigan--Welsh: at a semisimple (non-root-of-unity)\nparameter, exact Jones evaluation is $\\#\\mathrm{P}$-hard — so a\npolynomial-time evaluator collapses $\\mathrm{FP} = \\#\\mathrm{P}$.\n\nRef: [jaeger1990] https://doi.org/10.1017/S0305004100068936 ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.JonesComplexityCitations","kind":"class","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L124-L144","doc":"**Cited complexity layer** (hypotheses, not theorems of this\ndevelopment).  All four parameters are opaque `Prop`s:\n`semisimple` = $H_n(q_0)$ is semisimple (no radical pruning of the\nresolution tree), `JonesInFP` = exact Jones evaluation at $q_0$ is\npolynomial-time, `FPeqSharpP` = $\\mathrm{FP} = \\#\\mathrm{P}$,\n`PeqNP` = $\\mathrm{P} = \\mathrm{NP}$.  **No instance is declared**:\nthe fields are established literature results that Lean cannot\ncurrently express, carried honestly in the type. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.nontorsion_of_one_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.nontorsion_of_one_lt","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L101-L108","doc":"**The substrate point is non-torsion (sorry-free).**  Any real\n$q > 1$ — in particular $q_0 \\approx 1.10998$ — has no positive\npower equal to $1$, so no finite Kummer level applies to it:\n$q_0$ sits permanently outside the transparent set. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.chi_mod_vanishes_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.chi_mod_vanishes_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L94-L99","doc":"**Kummer arithmetic of the derived value (sorry-free).**  With\n$\\chi(A) = -6$, the mod-$n$ reduction of the obstruction vanishes\nexactly at the Jaeger--Vertigan--Welsh classically tractable\ntorsion levels $n \\mid 6$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.conclusion_of_faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.conclusion_of_faithful","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Faithfulness is the whole conjecture (sorry-free reduction).**\nGiven the derived non-vanishing, the faithful direction alone\nalready yields the conclusion.  Together with\n`sound_of_residual_ne_zero` and `equivalence_collapse`, this locates\nthe entire open content of `conj:qou-p-neq-np` in the single\nimplication `faithful`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.sound_of_residual_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.sound_of_residual_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L76-L82","doc":"**The soundness direction is free (sorry-free).**  Given the derived\nnon-vanishing, `P → r ≠ 0` holds for *any* proposition `P` — it\ncarries no information about computation.  The chippable half of\nthe equivalence chips to nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.equivalence_of_faithfulness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.equivalence_of_faithfulness","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L70-L74","doc":"The conjectured equivalence, *derived* from the two directions\n(sorry-free given the class hypotheses). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.faithful","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.faithful","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Faithfulness: a surviving residue forces the separation.  This\ndirection is the irreducible open kernel of `conj:qou-p-neq-np`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.sound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.sound","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L65-L65","doc":"Soundness: separation forces the obstruction residue to survive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness.mk","kind":"ctor","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.ResidueFaithfulness","kind":"class","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L58-L68","doc":"The two directions of the conjectured equivalence as separate named\nhypotheses (§3b-cond non-degenerate decomposition: the class carries\nthe genuine sub-claims, and the equivalence is *derived* from them\nby `Iff.intro`, never carried as a monolithic field).\n`PneqNP` is an opaque `Prop` pending a formal P/NP. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Information.equivalence_collapse","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Information.equivalence_collapse","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Information/PNeqNpEquivalence.lean#L49-L56","doc":"**Collapse of a conditioned equivalence (sorry-free).**  If `a`\nalready holds, then the assertion `a ↔ b` is equivalent to the bare\nassertion `b`.  Instantiated with `a := res ≠ 0` (derived, the\n$\\chi(A) = -6$ chain) and `b := P ≠ NP`, this says: the conjectured\nequivalence carries exactly the content $\\mathrm{P} \\neq \\mathrm{NP}$\n— no more, no less. ","signatureChunk":0}]}